diff --git a/docs/dev/TechnicalDebt.md b/docs/dev/TechnicalDebt.md
index 8f217818..5b04d207 100644
--- a/docs/dev/TechnicalDebt.md
+++ b/docs/dev/TechnicalDebt.md
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ Throughout the project, every function at every stage either **does exactly what
 - [libSceBluetoothHid](../../core/libs/prx/libSceBluetoothHid/Export.cpp) implements only the no-device path: initialization and callback and device registration succeed, the callback is never called because no device connects, and calls that need a connected device throw
 - [sceVideoOutOpen](../../core/libs/prx/libSceVideoOut/src/Output.cpp) validates the priority and CPU affinity that the open param requests for the VideoOut service thread but does not apply them: the port's present and vblank threads are host threads, and guest priorities and affinities do not reach host scheduling
 - Without `VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric` the shader recompiler [does not load the barycentric VGPRs](../../core/shader/recompiler/Translation/src/InstructionTranslator.cpp): [`v_interp_p1_f32` is dropped and `v_interp_p2_f32` reads the attribute Vulkan interpolated](../../core/shader/recompiler/Translation/src/AttributeInstructions.cpp), so pixel shaders that use the barycentrics for anything other than `v_interp` get wrong values.
-- [libSceAudio3d](../../core/libs/prx/libSceAudio3d/Export.cpp) - the port produces no sound: objects can be reserved but the library has no bed exports or `sceAudio3dObjectSetAttributes` to give them audio, so `sceAudio3dPortPush` only paces the queue at `granularity` samples per frame at 48 kHz. `sceAudio3dPortSetAttribute` accepts the late reverb level and the downmix spread attributes and ignores them
+- [libSceAudio3d](../../core/libs/prx/libSceAudio3d/Export.cpp) - the port produces no sound: it has no bed exports, object PCM renderer or mixing sink. `sceAudio3dObjectSetAttributes` validates the batch and the PCM/gain ABI but returns `NOT_SUPPORTED` for rendering attributes; only `RESET_STATE` succeeds on the empty object audio state and preserves its reservation. `sceAudio3dPortPush` paces empty frames at `granularity` samples per frame at 48 kHz, and `sceAudio3dPortFlush` submits any advanced frames and waits for all queued frames to finish. Their ABI, reset and drain semantics follow [shadPS4's Audio3d header/source](https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/tree/main/src/core/libraries/audio3d), not a PS5 hardware measurement. `sceAudio3dPortSetAttribute` still accepts the late reverb level and downmix spread attributes and ignores them
 - [libSceTextToSpeech2](../../core/libs/prx/libSceTextToSpeech2/Export.cpp) has no speech engine: `sceTextToSpeech2Initialize` fails and the other exports throw. PPSA01317 skips its narration set-up when initialization fails
 - [libSceAvPlayer](../../core/libs/prx/libSceAvPlayer/Export.cpp): `sceAvPlayerSetLogCallback` accepts a callback that is never called, as the player produces no log messages, and `sceAvPlayerSetAvailableBandwidth` has no effect, as it governs HLS sources, which `sceAvPlayerAddSource` does not implement.
 - [libSceHttp2](../../core/libs/prx/libSceHttp2/Export.cpp) - no request reaches the network, so `sceHttp2SetMinSslVersion` has no TLS connection to restrict and returns success for any `id`, like `sceHttp2SslEnableOption` (prosper returns the invalid-id error for an unknown one)
@@ -235,7 +235,7 @@ Throughout the project, every function at every stage either **does exactly what
 - [Shader registration](../../core/libs/prx/libSceAgcDriver/Execution/src/Driver/Shaders/ShaderRegistry.cpp) (libSceAgcDriver) - a shader header is accepted at any address: PPSA26344 passes headers 4 and 1 bytes past an 8-byte boundary; whether the console refuses an alignment is unknown
 - [sceNgs2VoiceControl sampler filter](../../core/libs/prx/libSceNgs2.native/src/Voice.cpp) (libSceNgs2.native) - param `0x1000000a`, its layout and meaning follow KytyPS5 only: location 1 type 1 is an RBJ low-pass biquad at the system sample rate after resampling, scaled by `level`, a set `channel_mask` bit bypasses that channel, type 0 turns the filter off. Other locations and types throw. The voice keeps playing a filter tail after its last block until the history is zero, with outputs below 1e-20 flushed to zero (a KytyPS5 choice); the console's tail length is unknown
 - [sceRtcGetDosTime, sceRtcSetDosTime](../../core/libs/prx/libSceRtc/Export.cpp) (libSceRtc) - bit layout from shadPS4 (PS4, the standard FAT date/time). A year outside 1980-2107 makes `GetDosTime` return `INVALID_YEAR` after writing 0 for an earlier one and `0xff9fbf7d` (2107-12-31 23:59:58, the largest encodable time) for a later one, and `SetDosTime` decodes the year as the unsigned 7-bit FAT field (1980-2107) without validating the fields, as the disassembly-derived [fpPS4](https://github.com/red-prig/fpPS4) reimplementation of the PS4 library does; not confirmed on a PS5 title, and shadPS4 instead masks out-of-range years into the packed value and sign-extends the 16-bit date
-- [sce::Json::InitParameter2](../../core/libs/prx/libSceJson2/Export.cpp) (libSceJson2) - layout inferred, not known: assumed to start with the allocator, its user data and the file buffer size, in that order, and the whole struct is assumed to fit in 40 bytes; `Initializer::initialize(InitParameter2)` ignores them as `initialize(InitParameter)` does
+- [sce::Json::InitParameter2](../../core/libs/prx/libSceJson2/Export.cpp) (libSceJson2) - SDK layout remains unknown. The observed caller reserves a 40-byte span and accesses the parameter only through imported methods. HLE retains its 24-byte API-owned representation; explicit virtual/RTTI setters select distinct policies in an alignment bit of the allocator token. Virtual allocation/free/notify use guest ABI slots 2/3/4 and preserve creating object/context/release code per block. The caller must keep its allocator object and code alive until all its storage is released. Default base notification is diagnostic only, and base deleting-destructor ownership is explicitly unsupported. No file-parser API is implemented; fileBufferSize is retained configuration, not a buffering promise.
 - [sceAjmBatchJobSetResampleParameters, sceAjmBatchJobGetResampleInfo](../../core/libs/prx/libSceAjm.native/src/Ajm.cpp) (libSceAjm) - the ratio is taken as decoded samples per output sample and num_samples as the decoded samples the resampler holds, both inferred from FMOD (Hades II); the console's interpolation is unknown, a 4-point Catmull-Rom is used. The flags argument is ignored, as in shadPS4 and Kyty
 - [scePlayerReviewDialogOpen, scePlayerReviewDialogGetResult](../../core/libs/prx/libSceCdlgPlayerReview/Export.cpp) (libSceCdlgPlayerReview) - the PS5-only dialog has no public reference: the parameter is not read and the result is assumed to start with the 32-bit common dialog result, as `sceWebBrowserDialogGetResult` assumes
 - [sceHttpWaitRequest](../../core/libs/prx/libSceHttp/Export.cpp) (libSceHttp) - the timeout is assumed to be in microseconds and a negative timeout to wait without limit; the invalid-value error for a null handle or event array or a non-positive event count is assumed, not measured. No request is ever pending, so the call waits for the timeout and returns 0 events, and a wait without limit throws
